{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"evaluated":11,"overflow":0,"schema":"epic_bug_screen_v1","tally":[{"citation":"Bug describes pre-existing O(N) full-store scan in llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py:delivered_children_manifest, not a defect in RP-04's operation-scoped config/auth composition or runtime binding changes.","ticket_id":"bb3a-c931-47ba-4808","title":"delivered-children manifest scans full store per child (delivered_now)","verdict":"B"},{"citation":"Epic AC requires 'Git and bridge factories preserve provider-native auth lifecycles and instantiate only the selected integration'; bridge fsck binding-drift audit is a defect in the bridge runtime binding composition that RP-04 S3/S5 must deliver.","ticket_id":"8656-01fe-6f74-44c9","title":"[binding-drift] bridge fsck found 1 audit finding(s)","verdict":"A"},{"citation":"RP-04 S2/S3 cut reconciler read/check paths to operation runtimes; completion_child_gate.py's full-store scan per child violates the immutable-snapshot and no-in-progress-reread contract, requiring the material_child_index snapshot wrapper to reach zero legacy ambient reads below approved seams.","ticket_id":"a3f5-5c19-faad-417b","title":"completion child gate scans full store per child","verdict":"A"},{"citation":"Enrich-drain gate budget overrun is a pre-existing queue/overlap subsystem concern; RP-04 does not claim to redesign the gate contract or its marker/budget semantics, only to compose immutable operation snapshots and bind auth/runtimes without reread.","ticket_id":"6148-5d81-8e80-41e8","title":"enrich-drain gate check runs 17-180x over its 20ms budget in steady state under sustained write load","verdict":"B"},{"citation":"Bug describes pytest configuration and test-harness timeout behavior; epic RP-04 concerns operation-scoped config resolution, provider auth composition, and credential handling — no overlap in subsystem or deliverable.","ticket_id":"797b-bbc4-01cf-42d5","title":"timeout_func_only leaves fixture setup/teardown hangs unguarded","verdict":"C"},{"citation":"Git runtime lifecycle and store I/O are pre-existing subsystem concerns; RP-04 composes GitRuntime bindings but does not change git-commit timeout or store-lock mechanics that this bug diagnoses.","ticket_id":"bd66-28a4-fd31-4c9f","title":"Diagnose temporary-store git commit timeout under suite load","verdict":"B"},{"citation":"Bug describes a defect in outbound_comments._diff_comments (live-search path) — same subsystem as RP-04 S7's config-ownership cutover, but a pre-existing comment-emission logic issue unrelated to operation-scoped configuration or provider-auth composition.","ticket_id":"9ebb-3114-4d0e-4528","title":"Parent-drift breadcrumb skipped in live-search path when child has no local comments","verdict":"B"},{"citation":"Bug describes a test/validation drift in backtest corpus pinning unrelated to RP-04's operation-scoped config/auth composition, provider binding, or secret handling.","ticket_id":"648b-7882-497f-45fc","title":"backtest --check-planning-corpus pin drifts: corpus=114, want 113","verdict":"C"},{"citation":"Bug describes a pre-existing CI workflow guard defect in `_optionality.yml` that RP-04 did not introduce; RP-04 S7.1/S7.2 own the AST ownership gate and CI parity checks, but this is a parallel gate-guard infrastructure issue, not a defect in RP-04's deliverable.","ticket_id":"d93e-92ce-e2d0-4033","title":"Guard the degradation-path test files in the Verified optionality lane","verdict":"B"},{"citation":"Bug describes a CI/workflow gate parity issue in test.yml; RP-04 epic scope is operation-scoped config/auth composition, provider bindings, and ownership gates for config reads—not GitHub Actions workflow guards or predates-gate parity.","ticket_id":"e818-564e-d3b6-4eaa","title":"Guard the golden-path gate scripts in the test.yml mirror lane","verdict":"C"},{"citation":"Epic AC 'every affected consumer receives an immutable projection/runtime binding and no in-progress operation rereads ambient state' — sign-review rereads store-wide tracker HEAD instead of subject's generation snapshot, violating immutability and operation-scoped isolation.","ticket_id":"a83f-6348-a08c-401d","title":"sign-review can never persist an attestation while any other ticket is being written: the sign fence compares store-wide tracker HEAD, not the subject's generation","verdict":"A"}],"ticket_id":"e215-ab23-ed6a-4791"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMPLETION_VERDICT","timestamp":1787444339365672001,"uuid":"fda156dd-f367-4575-8cd1-468b0979b7f2"}